Combined Domain Expansion: Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary
Executive Summary: We propose Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary, a domain that fuses Sukuna’s Malevolent Shrine mechanics (barrierless, sure-hit slashes) with Inumaki-style Cursed Speech echoes. Canonically, lethal domains “guarantee-hit” any cursed target inside
. Malevolent Shrine uniquely has no barrier shell and cannot be dispelled normally
, unleashing Cleave/Dismantle slashes on everything
. Cursed Speech compels targets to obey spoken commands
. In Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary, Wulf utters a command that echoes repeatedly, immobilizing or damaging foes while spectral wolf-fangs slash relentlessly. Below, we ground this on JJK lore, define its lore and mechanics in detail, present three vow-trade modes with counters, and compare it directly to Malevolent Shrine.

Canonical Mechanics
Domain Expansion Basics: A Domain Expansion is the apex technique of Jujutsu Sorcery
. Lethal domains are built with the caster’s cursed technique, amplifying all techniques to guarantee-hit targets (bypassing even Gojo’s Infinity)
. Malevolent Shrine is such a domain: it “hits anything within its effective range relentlessly”
 by using Cleave (living targets) and Dismantle (objects) slashes
. Notably, Sukuna’s domain has no enclosing barrier, so it cannot be destroyed normally – only by injuring Sukuna himself
.

Cursed Speech: Cursed Speech is an inherited technique that reinforces spoken commands with cursed energy, forcing listeners to comply
. Examples include paralyzing an enemy with “Don’t Move” or blasting them with “Explode”
. Its strength depends on the word and user skill
, and powerful words carry backlash. In JJK, clever tactics (like ear-protection
 or inner chants) can block curses. While no canon Domain uses Cursed Speech, fan concepts imagine domains where words echo (e.g., saying “freeze” halts movement until echoes fade)
.

Cursed Speech Domains (Fan Inspiration): One fan idea (“Echo Chamber”) has a domain where spoken commands echo continuously
. Another suggests repeating a word’s effect until the target dies
. These illustrate how echoing commands can be integrated: repeated commands immobilize foes, especially with a domain designed to reinforce each echo
.

Lore & Domain Name
Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary – Wulf Gegner’s ultimate domain. Upon activation, ancient runes and tribal motifs fill the air, forming a moonlit glade with spectral wolf-statues. The air trembles with Wulf’s low curse-word, which reverberates endlessly. This domain reflects Wulf’s cold precision and twisted devotion: ghostly wolf-fangs and bones form the shrine, while haunting whispers (some in Leora’s voice) echo off the stone. Wulf’s presence is as still as a hunter at the center of this wailing lair. Inside Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary, every syllable of his curse is a command of doom, amplified by lupine fury.

Example: Wulf’s amber eyes flash as he softly intones a single word. The sanctuary’s shadows stir into phantom wolves that snarl. The word “Stay” repeats like a chant, and anyone within must halt in terror as spectral claws descend – combining the domain’s unerring slashes with a paralyzing command.

Detailed Mechanics
Activation: Wulf forms a unique hand sign and utters a trigger word or phrase (e.g. “Stasis!”). This activates the domain instantaneously (no full incantation needed, akin to Sukuna’s sudden expansion
). The domain unfolds around him, extending up to ~100 meters (example) by default, with no physical barrier shell (barrierless)
.

Barrier Status: The domain is open-barrier (like Malevolent Shrine
). It does not require enveloping space; the effect can extend into surrounding area. This means ordinary barriers cannot block its effects. However, this makes Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary just as indestructible as Malevolent Shrine: it can only be ended by injuring Wulf sufficiently
 or by Wulf choosing to cancel it.

Range: By default, Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary covers roughly a 100m radius. Wulf can adjust this via binding vows. For instance, he can shrink it to focus power on a smaller zone (like Sukuna did to strike Gojo’s outer shell
) or expand it (at a cost, as below). In Shibuya, Sukuna’s shrine reached ~140m
, so our 100m is a reasonable baseline example.

Guaranteed-Hit Logic: Any cursed target inside is doomed. Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary inherits the sure-hit factor
: as long as Wulf sustains the domain, the combined effect cannot “miss”. The echoing command forces the target to comply or suffer the curse (functionally unavoidable, especially if unaware of countermeasures
). Simultaneously, spectral wolf-slashes (animated spirit weapons or fang-projectiles) continuously assault everything in range. These slashes mirror Cleave/Dismantle – flesh and spirit are cut, objects are shattered. The synergy: as soon as a word takes effect, the wolves strike, ensuring at least one of the attacks (word or fang) connects. If Wulf vows away guaranteed-hit, targets might dodge with sufficient barrier (see Modes/Counters).

Cursed Words & Wolf Attacks: Each word triggers in two layers. First, the verbal command echoes through the domain, applying its effect repeatedly (in line with fan concepts
). E.g., “Don’t move!” loops until the domain ends or target breaks free. Second, simultaneously the command releases a coordinated assault of spectral wolf-fangs. Mechanically, uttering a word spawns one volley of slashes; if Wulf continues speaking (or repeats words), it can produce sequential waves. Timing example: upon “Freeze,” a wave of ghostly wolves leaps forward. After a pause, Wulf might add “Now!” causing another strike. Each wave is instant and automatically hits (the domain’s innate curse grants no “misses”
).

Interaction with Infinity/Other Domains: Because Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary is lethal and barrierless, it can overtake many domains. Like Sukuna, it can override domains with weaker barriers
. The slash attacks, being domain-effects, bypass Infinity
. The echo commands, however, can be countered: advanced sorcerers (e.g., Gojo-level) could block the auditory curse by manipulating their brain’s ears
, preventing the speech aspect while still facing the slashes. In a domain clash (two domains overlapping), Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary behaves like Malevolent Shrine: if its boundary oversteps a barrier (as Sukuna did to Void
), it can overwhelm the weaker domain. Gojo’s Infinity would halt any non-sure-hit effect – but here, unless Wulf sacrifices that effect (see Modes), all attacks are guaranteed.

Energy Cost: Opening Fenrir’s Echo Sanctuary consumes an enormous amount of cursed energy (on par with Sukuna’s renowned expansions
). We estimate as example: sustaining a 100m radius for 1 minute might require ~100 “energy units” (arbitrary), making multiple expansions very taxing. Each spoken command also costs additional energy (stronger words cause more backlash
). Under heavy use (e.g. continuous echoing and slashing), Wulf would quickly exhaust himself – in line with the risky nature of domain use
.

